# Contributing

Thanks for helping improve **{{ project_name }}**.

This project uses:

- [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for Python + dependency management
- [`ruff`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/) for linting and formatting
- [`pyright`](https://pypi.org/project/pyright/) for static type checking
- [`pytest`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/) for testing
- [`poethepoet`](https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet) tasks (run via `poe`)
- [`pre-commit`](https://pre-commit.com/) to run fast checks before commits
- [`bandit`](https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) and [`pip-audit`](https://pypi.org/project/pip-audit/) for security checks
- [`mkdocs`](https://www.mkdocs.org/) for documentation and [`Material for MkDocs`](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/) theme.

## Quick start

### Prerequisites

- Python {{ min_python_version }}+
- [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)

### Setup

```bash
uv sync --all-groups
```

Notes:

- `--all-groups` installs both the `dev` and `docs` dependency groups.
- If you only want the development tooling (no docs), you can use:

```bash
uv sync --group dev
```

> All the poe task below are defined in `pyproject.toml`.
> You can either run them via `uv run poe <task>` or install `poethepoet` (`uv tool install poethepoet`) and run them via `poe <task>`.

### All Poe Tasks

| Task         | Description                                                                  |
|--------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `clean`      | Clean build/test caches and generated artifacts                              |
| `fix`        | Run ruff formatting + lint fixes                                             |
| `check`      | Run ruff (lint + format check), pyright (type-check), and pytest (unit tests)|
| `security`   | Run bandit and pip-audit (security checks)                                   |
| `docs`       | Run mkdocs (documentation)                                                   |
| `gen`        | Run git-changelog (regenerate CHANGELOG.md from git history)                 |
| `test-pyall` | Run pytest suite across all supported Python versions                        |
| `pre-commit` | Run pre-commit hooks on all files (useful to test after pre-commit failure)  |
| `ci`         | Full suite intended for CI (useful to test after CI failure)                 |

### Testing
#### Multi-version testing
Project uses `uv` with `--python` flag to create isolated environments for testing across multiple python versions.

Run below command to run tests for inidividual python versions:
```bash
{%- for v in supported_python_versions %}
poe test-py{{ v | replace('.', '') }}
{%- endfor %}
```

or run below command to run tests across all supported python versions:
```bash
poe test-pyall
```

#### Tag based testing
Tests can be tagged using `@pytest.mark.<tagname>` decorator.

To run tests with specific tags:
```bash
pytest -m "<tagname>"
```

Project defines `integration` tag for integration tests.

To run only integration tests:
```bash
poe test-integration
```

All untagged tests are considered unit tests.

> If you are adding a new tag, make sure to update `test-unit` poe task in `pyproject.toml` to exclude the new tag.

### Documentation

Documentation is built using [MkDocs](https://www.mkdocs.org/) and the [Material for MkDocs](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/) theme.

```bash
uv sync --group docs
uv run poe docs
```

To serve docs locally:

```bash
uv run poe docs-serve
```

> `docs` task also runs unit tests before building the docs. This is required for coverage reporting in docs.

## Typical developer flow

1. Install dependencies:


1. Install dependencies:

```bash
uv sync --all-groups
```

2. Install pre-commit hooks (once):

```bash
uv run pre-commit install
```

3. Make your change.

4. Auto-fix formatting + lint issues:

```bash
uv run poe fix
```

5. Run the standard checks:

```bash
uv run poe check
```

6. If your change touches docs, run:

```bash
uv run poe docs-build
```

7. If your change might affect integration behavior, run:

```bash
uv run poe test-integration
```

8. If you have added a new dependency, make sure to run:

```bash
uv sync --all-groups
uv run poe security
```

## pre-commit

`pre-commit` runs quick, local checks before you commit.

It includes basic file hygiene checks and runs `uv run poe pre-commit` (Ruff
format + Ruff lint fixes).

Install a one-time git hook to run pre-commit on every commit:

```bash
uv run pre-commit install
```

To run all hooks manually:

```bash
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

